WEBVTT

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:25.170
Don't... don't... go. Stay...

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.220
Hey!

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.350
Huh?

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:53.440
His key's here, so I guess he should be back soon.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.610
Hello!

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.570
God, she's back.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:00:59.700
That woman...

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.870
Ah, the heiress journalist.

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.250
Who's that?

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.370
You don't know her, Ishii?

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:08.630
Her father's the Chief of Police.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:09.250
What?

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:12.760
If we leak any info, it could hinder our investigations,

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.260
Come on, just a bit.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:17.640
yet we can't just ignore her because of who her father is.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:19.760
Sorry, but we can't just-

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.760
Either way, she's an eyesore.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:22.010
Just try and be careful, okay?

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:22.890
Okay...

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:26.690
Oh, Detective Goto-

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:27.690
Go to hell.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.110
May I have some comments from you regarding your investigations?

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:32.360
Please.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:36.900
I have nothing to say to those who rely on their father's name to gain information.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:40.490
My father is <i>just</i> my father. He's got nothing to do with this.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:50.420
Detective Goto, do you believe in ghosts?

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:51.380
What?

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:56.380
There are still so many things in this world that can't be explained by science.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.180
Ghosts, eh?

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:03.890
The law doesn't acknowledge their existence, but personally, I believe they do.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.390
Please, take a look at this.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:16.240
This is a job for <i>him</i>.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:19.360
Sorry, coming in.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:24.910
You scared me.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:28.960
Um, you're that detective from the other day, aren't you?

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:31.460
Yes, that would be me.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:33.710
If you're looking for Saito-kun, he's not here at the moment.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:35.340
So it seems.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.170
I guess I'll wait for him here.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:41.050
I'm Ozawa Haruka.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:41.800
What?

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.430
Oh, I'm Goto.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.730
He sure is late...

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:54.820
He's a master at making people wait for him, yet always refuses to wait himself.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.740
He's always been like that.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.240
Have you known each other long?

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:11.460
Yeah, I've known him since he was a kid.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:17.960
Police officer...

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.550
A child...

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:22.640
What?

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.050
A child...

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.890
...is about to be killed.

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.480
Um...

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.570
Oh, sorry.

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:40.030
I kind of dozed off.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:43.660
Dozing off? That's nothing new for you.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.780
Ah! Saito-kun!

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.660
Where have you been?

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.910
I went home to return a book.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:55.170
You could have at least left me a note or something.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:57.210
Why do I need to tell you when I'm going home?

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:00.260
It's none of your business, right?

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:00.800
What?

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.430
Well, you don't, but...

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.430
So? Who was here first?

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.810
So, what kind of trouble are you in today?

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:13.940
Hey, I'm not a troublemaker, so don't call me that.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.440
True.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:17.690
As long as you understand.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.940
You're trouble itself.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:22.530
What?

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:29.080
I missed the last bus because I was working overtime.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:33.710
The assistant manager, Nakahara Tatsuya-san, drove me to the station.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.750
This road...

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.710
It's a shortcut to the station.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:43.590
But isn't there a haunted tunnel along this way?

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:44.800
Ghosts?

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.470
They don't scare me at all.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:50.220
Bring it on.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:53.810
But once we entered the tunnel...

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.700
Hang on tight.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.070
Okay!

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.290
That's quite a dependable assistant manager you have there.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:23.960
Apparently, he's not afraid of ghosts or any other eerie phenomena for that matter.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:29.800
Sounds like he'd make a far better boyfriend than a certain someone, right, Haruka-chan?

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.850
That's not the point.

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:35.060
So, about your boyfriend...

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:37.730
Not you too, Saito-kun!

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.690
What do you want from me?

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:45.070
I want you to check and see if any of the ghosts have attached themselves to us.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:51.580
You don't have any ghosts with you.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:56.250
However, without seeing the driver, Nakahara Tatsuya, in person,

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:59.330
I've no way of telling whether any ghosts attached themselves to him.

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:01.090
Will you see him?

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:03.380
Only if my conditions are met.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.300
Money again?

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:07.130
Hey, Yakumo!

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:10.640
You intend to charge a sweet girl like her?

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.550
You sure are greedy.

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:14.890
I'm on a tight budget.

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:21.940
Partially because someone refused to pay me a penny even though I helped him in his investigations.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:25.070
That's that and this is this. They're two different things.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.080
What do you think?

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:36.700
The building in the background... It's a garage, right?

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:38.160
Yeah, that's right.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.580
It's not your ordinary garage either.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:44.000
The owner is Hayami Tooru, 38 years old.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:49.590
A bastard who'll fix <i>any</i> car for money.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:55.350
This underground garage came to light when we were investigating a hit-and-run.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:07:01.850
When the bungling idiots handling the case went to the garage, the owner had already fled.

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:04.610
Do you know who this boy is?

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.070
He was a grade-schooler who lived in the city.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:11.610
He went missing two months ago and was never found.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:14.320
So basically, you're asking me to question this boy's ghost,

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:18.910
in the hope that it will lead us to information resulting in the arrest of Hayami Tooru, right?

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:26.130
Well, you still owe me for that case, so you really have no choice.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.180
Where have you been?

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.340
And what the hell is that for?

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:36.970
This is what's known as a shovel.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:38.640
I know that, idiot!

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:41.020
I was asking you what you plan to do with it!

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:48.030
Hey, help dig, will you?

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:51.320
I already am helping.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:55.070
You'd better make sure you earn your salary.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:08:00.120
So what are the chances that the boy from the photo is still alive?

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:07.630
Though it's extremely uncommon, there are times when a soul temporarily leaves a living body.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.930
I hope that's what happened.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.430
You've changed.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:22.430
And so have you. You've put on some weight.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:24.230
Are you preparing yourself for hibernation?

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:26.270
Quit joking around.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:34.700
Say, that Haruka seems like a nice girl.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:36.740
That again?

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:38.830
Look, I'm being serious here.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.830
When you don't like something, you clam up, eh?

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:48.670
Hey, Yakumo.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:53.670
Unfortunately, your wish didn't come true.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:04.180
Regarding the body you dug up the other day,

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:06.560
he suffered from subconjunctival hemorrhaging

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.520
and had rope burn on his neck.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:10.770
All these are typical of strangulation.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:13.280
So, it wasn't a car accident?

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:19.280
Although there were tire marks in the abdominal region and he'd sustained damages to his organs,

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.580
those injuries wouldn't have proved fatal.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:27.210
So basically, he was strangled to death after being run over.

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:31.590
That's just cruel!

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:35.300
You aren't exactly suited to this line of work, are you?

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:36.430
What?

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:39.180
You have too many feelings for the victims.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.760
Is that so?

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:47.390
My job isn't exactly one of my hobbies either - unlike some disgusting geezer.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:50.230
Who is it?

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:51.770
It's me, Hijikata.

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:53.900
I just wanted to tell you something.

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:56.190
Cut the preface and just give me the facts.

00:09:56.190 --> 00:10:01.240
The owner of the garage, Hayami Tooru, has just been arrested.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.040
How is he?

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.500
He's fine.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:13.000
He's got no ghosts attached to him.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.420
Thank goodness!

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:18.930
Assistant Manager, I'm sorry for requesting something so strange of you.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.680
Nah, it's made me feel at ease now.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.510
Still, this is a strange room.

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:29.020
Rather than a film club, it reminds me of a secret base I made when I was a kid.

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:33.520
By the way, just for future reference, may I ask you something?

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:34.900
What is it?

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:39.150
What would you have done if there really was a ghost attached to me?

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:41.530
I would've tried to persuade them to leave verbally.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.530
Even though they're ghosts?

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:47.540
I don't have the ability to perform exorcisms or purifications.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.540
Nor do I favor such methods.

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:12.730
Your boyfriend's not coming back, is he?

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:19.490
We should be heading to the restaurant soon or we'll both be late.

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:23.990
You're suspicious of Nakahara Tatsuya?

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:28.500
But the owner of the garage, Hayami, has already been arrested.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:33.500
Besides, isn't Nakahara that courageous assistant manager from that udon restaurant?

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:39.300
He was noticeably unsettled when he saw that photo.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:43.010
Anyone would become unsettled after unexpectedly seeing a photo like that.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:51.890
However, she said he was extremely calm when he came face-to-face with those ghosts in the tunnel.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:52.940
I see.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:56.770
It is certainly odd for someone to be more afraid of a photo than the real thing.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:12:00.780
Rather than a fear of ghosts,

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:05.780
it may be that he either recognizes the boy or the location where it was taken.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:07.030
You think he recognizes him?

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:11.750
That, or Nakahara's involved in the murder.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:15.540
In that case, it might be worth looking into-

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:16.880
Hey, hold on a sec.

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:20.460
Are you sure?

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:23.930
Yes. Apparently, Hayami Tooru confessed.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:26.890
Yakumo, it's just as you suspected.

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:28.720
Nakahara Tatsuya is a suspect.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:33.350
Two months ago, he hit that boy.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:36.730
In addition to asking Hayami Tooru to fix his car, he-

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:42.150
He murdered the still breathing victim and buried him...

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.740
to cover up the accident.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:46.950
That's right.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:48.870
He's still there, right?

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:51.240
Keep him there at all costs.

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:55.210
When did I become one of your subordinat-

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:59.000
Hey, what's wrong?

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.460
Goto-san, please get here as soon as possible.

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:02.420
What?!

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:03.380
Hey, what happened?

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:13.270
Perhaps that's your boyfriend.

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:17.020
I guess we shouldn't have left without saying goodbye.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:18.900
Aren't you going to answer that?

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:26.860
The other day, he said that he didn't have to tell me his movements every time he goes somewhere.

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:29.030
Now, we're even.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.790
The lights were red just now!

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:42.920
I can't move...

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:44.420
What?

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:46.420
It's... as if...

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:49.340
I'm... being controlled... by someone.

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:51.220
Wh-What are you saying?!

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:58.850
Save me, Saito-kun!

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.860
It's rare for you to welcome me.

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:08.070
Nakahara Tatsuya isn't here.

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:09.240
He's with her.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:12.370
Her? You mean Haruka-chan?

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:15.200
Apparently, they're heading east on the national highway.

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:16.620
Don't tell me...

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:23.340
Save me...

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:26.460
I-It was all my fault.

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:28.550
Nakahara-san, hang in there!

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:36.220
Drive up alongside it.

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:37.680
What are you planning to do?

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:40.480
I'm going to try and persuade the boy's ghost from his course of action.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:41.900
Are you serious?

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:13.050
Stop the car at once.

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:20.060
Stop! Once you enter that tunnel, you won't be able to return.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:32.820
Why can't you understand me?

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:42.920
Damn it. If we enter the tunnel at this speed, we'll crash straight into the bend inside it!

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.420
S-Save me!

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:56.680
Hey, Yakumo.

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:01.020
You owe me one.

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:24.960
Stop!

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:45.730
Are you okay?

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:47.770
Yes...

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:51.480
Wait!

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:52.610
What's wrong?

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:54.990
Hey, Yakumo, where are you going?!

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:28.020
I'm sorry.

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:30.730
I...

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:56.470
Saito-kun?

00:17:57.430 --> 00:18:00.390
From time to time, I feel frustrated.

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:04.060
I don't save anyone.

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:07.640
You... or that boy's ghost.

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:11.980
I can only see them. There's nothing that I can do.

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:49.560
Actually, Yakumo asked me to come today.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:55.070
He asked if there was something I could do since there are many ghosts that cannot rest in this area.

00:18:55.530 --> 00:19:00.950
Even so, the only thing I can do is to give them an invocation to Buddha.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.880
Yakumo said he felt frustrated?

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:15.000
Yes.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.760
I see, that Yakumo...

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:23.090
I was the one who named him Yakumo.

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:29.100
When multiple clouds overlap with one another, it's known as "Yakumo."

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:37.610
When I saw his red eye, I thought that his life would be full of obstacles,

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:42.570
just like the many layers of clouds that block the sunlight.

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:45.830
So that's why you named him Yakumo...

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:51.080
I named him that hoping that he'd be able to overcome them all.

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:58.130
He's probably managed to overcome another obstacle, one of many still to come.

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:13.140
I believe that one day his heart will be as clear as this sky.

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:15.650
So do I...

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:16.980
Huh?

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:22.240
I want to help him.

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:26.660
I'm counting on you.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:28.950
Okay.

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:53.940
My, this is...

00:21:09.240 --> 00:21:11.370
Who are they?

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:16.000
Ayaka... Why?

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:18.380
Why won't you come back?

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:21.960
Let's hope the next one will work out, Sensei.

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:27.260
It will be your turn soon, Yakumo.
